  "original_summary": "\r\n1. Inputs:\r\n- `ModuleElement mdle`: An instance of the `ModuleElement` class, which presumably represents some information about a Java module.\r\n\r\n2. Outputs:\r\n- A `List` of `String` objects. If the `config` object's `keywords` property is set to `true`, the list will contain a single string, which is the qualified name of the `ModuleElement` followed by the string \" module\". If the `config` object's `keywords` property is `false`, the list will be an empty list.\r\n\r\n3. Business Purpose:\r\nThe purpose of this method is to return a list of meta keywords for a given Java module. The meta keywords are simply the qualified name of the module followed by the string \" module\". If the configuration object does not have the `keywords` property set to `true`, then an empty list is returned instead."
